# Frontend UX Rules

## Sidebar 3-Step Wizard

**Flow:** Context (step 0) → Usage (step 1) → Sounds (step 2)

Implemented in `frontend/src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx`.

### Step Definitions

| Step | Section component | Valid card types | Prerequisite |
| ---- | ----------------- | ---------------- | ------------ |
| 0 — Context | `ContextSection` | `model-analysis`, `3d-model`, `audio`, `freeform` | — |
| 1 — Usage | `UsageSection` | `scenario`, `text`, `freeform` | `parentContextOriginalIndex` set |
| 2 — Sounds | `SoundGenerationSection` | sound configs | `parentUsageOriginalIndex` set |

### Key State (Sidebar.tsx)

| Variable | Type | Purpose |
| -------- | ---- | ------- |
| `currentStep` | `0 \| 1 \| 2` | Active wizard step |
| `activeContextOriginalIndex` | `number \| null` | Which context card is active / expanded |
| `activeUsageOriginalIndex` | `number \| null` | Which usage card is active |
| `bypassedUsage` | `boolean` | User skipped the usage step entirely |

### UIStore Fields

| Field | Purpose |
| ----- | ------- |
| `activeSoundParentIndex` | `null` = skip flow, show all sounds regardless of step |
| `isInSoundsStep` | Gates `unifiedSoundscapeData` — sounds must not render before this is `true` |

## Card Linkage System

Cards use **original index fields** that never change even when cards are reordered:

- `parentContextOriginalIndex` — links a usage card to its parent context card
- `parentUsageOriginalIndex` — links a sound to its parent usage card

Usage cards are filtered in step 1 by `activeContextOriginalIndex`.
Sound cards are filtered in step 2 by `activeUsageOriginalIndex`.

### Negative Index Namespace

Audio-type context cards (type `audio`) use:
```
parentUsageOriginalIndex = -(N + 1)
```
where `N` is the context card's original index. This distinguishes audio context linkage from
normal usage linkage (which uses non-negative integers).

## Freeform (Bypass) Cards

| Trigger | Card type | Effect |
| ------- | --------- | ------ |
| "Skip context" | `freeform` context | No `parentContextOriginalIndex`; auto-advances to step 1 on creation |
| "Skip usage" | `freeform` usage | Has `parentContextOriginalIndex`; auto-advances to step 2 on creation |

Default names: `"Untitled context"` / `"Untitled usage"` — editable inline via `display_name`.

## Navigation Guard Pattern

`prevContextLength` and `prevUsageLength` are `useRef` values initialised to the **current card
count at component mount**:

```typescript
const prevContextLength = useRef(contextCards.length)   // init to current count
```

This prevents re-triggering auto-advance when a section remounts during back-navigation.

**Do not convert these refs to state.** They must be non-reactive to work correctly — reactive
state would re-run the effect and falsely trigger navigation.

## FAB Navigation Rules

- Context FAB → advances to Usage (or directly to Sounds for `audio`/`freeform` context cards)
- Usage FAB → advances to Sounds
- FABs are hidden when the target step has no valid destination card

## Breadcrumb Tooltips

| Breadcrumb | Shows |
| ---------- | ----- |
| Context | All context card `display_name` + `(pending)` if not yet analysed |
| Usage | All usage card `display_name` + `(pending)` if no result/foley |
| Sounds | Grouped by usage parent; each sound name + `(pending)` if not in `generatedSounds` |

## Card Expand / Reduce

Expanded card view shows linked child cards and sounds as a placeholder list.
Expand state is **local component state** — do not persist it in any Zustand store.

## Before / After Generation States

Components should render differently based on whether a sound has been generated:

| State | Condition | UI |
| ----- | --------- | -- |
| Before generation | Sound ID not in `generatedSounds` (soundscapeStore) | Generation button + pending badge |
| After generation | Sound ID in `generatedSounds` | WaveSurfer waveform player + re-generate option |

`isInSoundsStep` (uiStore) must be `true` before rendering any generated sound content.

## page.tsx — Intentionally Large

`frontend/src/app/page.tsx` imports 17+ stores and wires all global effects and callbacks.
This is the **orchestration layer** by design — it owns the single-mount lifecycle contract for
the entire app.

Do not decompose store subscriptions into child components to "clean it up". Distributing them
would scatter ownership, break mount ordering, and make global side effects unpredictable.
